# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# An input no caller binds travels absent to the method that reads it, and
# that method reads its own lexical source. g1 reads other. hop only hands
# it on, and so does h0, the definition makeUse returns. inner calls it and
# names no other: g1 reads the unit's, 9, at the call: 5 + 10. After
# other: 20 the same call gives 5 + 21. over has its own other, 0: a
# supplied zero is present, 5 + 1. From the root the unit's other is the
# root's own binding. Entry 7.
int: other 9

fn: g1 () int
    return: other + 1
end: g1

fn: hop () int
    return: g1()
end: hop

fn: makeUse (int: k) fn: () int
    fn: h0 () int
        return: k + hop()
    return: h0

@: u0 makeUse(5)

fn: inner () int
    return: u0()
end: inner

fn: over () int
    int: other 0
    return: u0()
end: over

int: a inner()
int: b over()
other: 20
int: c inner()
int: d u0()
int: ok 7
if: a != 15 || b != 6 || c != 26 || d != 26
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
